<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves down $109 mln in Nov.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves down $109 mln in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Net international reserves of Ecuador's Central Bank fell 6 percent, or $109 million, in November, to $1.652 billion, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In October, net reserves reached $1.761 billion, an increase of $71 million from September.</p>
<p>In November 1995 reserves were $1.618 billion.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.557 billion at the end of last year, down $145 million from the end of 1994.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
